      "title": "DepthPro2 — Image to Depth",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## DepthPro2 — Image to Depth\n\nMetric depth (meters) from a single photo with [Apple Depth Pro 2](https://huggingface.co/apple/DepthPro2).\n\n**Loader**\n- `model`: `depthpro2-s/b/l/h` download automatically into `models/depthpro2` on first use (S: 97 MB, H+: 3.5 GB). Larger = sharper and steadier.\n- `precision`: `auto` = bf16 on GPU, fp32 on CPU. `fp8` halves weight memory again (~7% depth deviation); `bf16` is near-lossless (~0.7%).\n\n**Estimate**\n- `f_px`: focal length in pixels of the input image; `0` estimates it automatically. Depth in meters scales linearly with focal length — set it if you know it (EXIF 35mm-equivalent: `f_px = f35 * sqrt(W² + H²) / 43.27`).\n- `max_size`: longest side processed; `0` = native resolution (sharpest edges, most memory).\n\n**Outputs**\n- `depth_image`: normalized inverse depth, near white / far black (preview / ControlNet).\n- `depth_meters`: raw metric depth `(T, H, W)`, `inf` at sky.\n- `focal_length_px`: focal used, in pixels of the input.\n\nWeights are licensed for **non-commercial research only** (Apple AMLR)."
      ]
    },
